From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 17:53:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: tolerate stripped-action references in built-in
 keymaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

load_asset_allow_partial_failure gains a source: Option<KeybindSource>
param and now log::warn!+drops danglers instead of bailing. The three
load_default_keymap unwraps in zed.rs switch to it via .log_err() so a
keymap referencing actions from a removed crate (collab, channel, …) no
longer crashes startup. Test call sites updated for the new signature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs         |  3 +-
 crates/editor/src/edit_prediction_tests.rs |  1 +
 crates/editor/src/editor_tests.rs          |  1 +
 crates/search/src/buffer_search.rs         |  3 ++
 crates/settings/src/keymap_file.rs         | 24 ++++++++++++++--
 crates/vim/src/test/vim_test_context.rs    |  3 +-
 crates/zed/src/zed.rs                      | 33 ++++++++++++++--------
 7 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

